# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is a per-machine setting that cannot be enforced across a team,
# and with it enabled the working tree is CRLF while every tool in this repo
# expects LF. That mismatch is not cosmetic: `prettier --check` reported ~700
# files as failing when only one genuinely was, which is indistinguishable from
# noise and trained everyone to ignore it. Shell scripts are worse — a .sh file
# with CRLF fails to parse under strict shells with an opaque `$'\r': command
# not found`.
#
# Pinning eol=lf here overrides core.autocrlf, so every checkout is identical
# regardless of platform or local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executable scripts must be LF or they will not run.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary formats: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary

# Mark external vendored code for GitHub linguist
# This excludes it from language statistics and diffs by default
external/activities.next/** linguist-vendored
